-- title:
--   The canonical support-pair map on an actual orbit atlas
-- statement:
--   Fix support-torsion data $D$ for a finite graph $H$, with odd carrier base $m=2q+1$. Let continuous marker-box data have scales $L_j\ge1$ and separation parameter $S\ge24$. Choose a distinguished coordinate $i$, height $K$, and one normalized contraction family for every positive interval width at most $6L_i$.
--
--   For each action point $x$ and real lattice coordinate $z\in\mathbb R^d$, the canonical projected map first evaluates the resulting rank-$(d+1)$ skeleton on the cell containing $z$, then projects its carrier value into the support-pair space of $H$. This definition fixes the literal map whose continuity, finite dependence, and covariance are established by subsequent results.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (2026), Section(s) 3–6; https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.39824v1. This item is auxiliary infrastructure of the accompanying formalization; its implementation definitions are not asserted to be separately numbered in the paper. Original Lean module AbelianTargets/ActualProjectedOriginLocality.lean, selected declaration lines 43-48; SHA-256 c9244e8e24a2cd4c48e774a4b3de38b84d034712c8cb55b82c0770d9b2fe3d27. Selected spans are from the final generated manifest. The original source snapshot is local; no public repository URL or commit was available.

